---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="Gentech Media Solutions is an IT-led agency helping startups and growing companies with technology, media, and operations."
>
	<section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-20">
		<p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide text-amber-500 uppercase">About</p>
		<h1 class="mt-2 font-display text-4xl font-semibold text-navy-950">
			Why we work across IT, media, and management
		</h1>
		<div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-navy-700/90">
			<p>
				Most growing companies don't have a "technology problem" or a "marketing problem" in isolation — they have a
				handful of connected gaps that different vendors keep solving in isolation. An IT contractor fixes the
				infrastructure without understanding the brand. A marketing agency runs a campaign without knowing what the
				product roadmap or the team's bandwidth actually looks like. A management consultant designs a process no
				one has the tooling to support.
			</p>
			<p>
				Gentech Media Solutions exists to close that gap. We lead with IT — because reliable systems are the
				foundation everything else depends on — and build out from there into media and operational support, for
				startups and growing companies that need more than a single vendor can offer, but aren't ready for (or
				don't want) three separate ones.
			</p>
			<p>
				That means the same team that helps you get your infrastructure and tooling right is also thinking about how
				that shows up in your marketing, and how it fits the way your operations actually run day to day. Less
				hand-off, less re-explaining your business from scratch to every new vendor.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="mt-16 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
			<div class="rounded-2xl border border-navy-900/10 bg-white p-6">
				<p class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-navy-950">Who we work with</p>
				<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-navy-700/80">
					Startups and growing companies that need real technical, creative, and operational support without
					building out a full internal team for each function yet.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="rounded-2xl border border-navy-900/10 bg-white p-6">
				<p class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-navy-950">How we start</p>
				<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-navy-700/80">
					A conversation about where you actually are — what's working, what's fragile, and what you need first —
					before we talk about scope.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="rounded-2xl border border-navy-900/10 bg-white p-6">
				<p class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-navy-950">What stays consistent</p>
				<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-navy-700/80">
					One team, one context, across IT, media, and management — so decisions in one area account for the
					others.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="mt-16 text-center">
			<a
				href="/contact"
				class="inline-block rounded-full bg-navy-950 px-7 py-3.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition-colors hover:bg-amber-500 hover:text-navy-950"
			>
				Get in touch
			</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
